{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/393373-the-strangest-thing-you-used-on-wod","id":393373,"title":"The Strangest thing you used on WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-04T20:43:32-08:00","id":393373,"title":"The Strangest thing you used on WoD","content":"I dont mean bygones and such..but so bizarre strange things you woudnt belive to normally see in a game. such as Elvis, roots to cause Orgasms, Werewolves at furry cons, Fear and Loathing in X, Causing vampires to Sparkle. etc..<br /> <br /> i mean the most bizarre/pop culture thing you seen on a game and yet the most hilarous","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T01:40:05-08:00","id":393514,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it's not the strangest, but it definetley is the freshest. Last night one of my old friends came back into our long running Ahadi game with a new character. The character was patterned after Delboy from Only Fools and Horses. Then he appeared in the session and went crazy. The faces of the rest of the cast were brilliant and I spent a good 15 minutes just listening to him talk to the cast and laughing so hard it hurt. I'm sure that this time next year, they will all be millionaires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T04:30:29-08:00","id":393647,"title":"","content":"Wasn't roots, was a powder made from crushed vampire fangs, but that did happen once. Had a blood magician create a new kind of humoculus out of a bag of gummy bears, they would swell up to the size of a small dog then jump on the target and explode getting them all sticky and causing it to be difficult to move. Last but not least, a care bear made an appearance in an umbral realm to aid the players once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T05:16:38-08:00","id":393660,"title":"","content":"Werewolf first session ever - teenager times. Silver Fang player get a lot of resources dots and he wanted to became something like batman ... even with wolf signal... silly silly session and silly ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:41:10-08:00","id":393937,"title":"","content":"I played in a vampire game where we got stuck in the shadowlands thanks to a horribly botched thaumaturgical ritual (the Tremere in our coterie had some necromantic knowledge, but not enough, apparently). We got chased around by spectres through a nightmare wasteland, hid out among some down on their luck renegades, and got pointed to a haunt where we might be able to return to the skinlands. On our way we encountered a very strange looking thing that appeared sort of like drunken confusion of a scorpion and centipede that was feeding on mangled wraiths. We were able to bargain with it by feeding it some ripped up spectre corpus, but to this day I have no idea what it was supposed to be. It seemed too smart to be a plasmic, and if it was a heavily moliated wraith it was behaving very strangely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T12:41:25-08:00","id":394045,"title":"","content":"The first VtM campaign I played in was set in Memphis, and Elvis was the prince of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:08:55-08:00","id":394159,"title":"","content":"Though this was in a Requiem game, my character managed to dominate and ghoul a rat and use it as a &quot;rat compass&quot; to find things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}